      "role": "user",
      "content": "I see. So, in a practical sense for my students, if they were aiming to create a very convincing, high-credibility witness for their trial, would you suggest they stick strictly to Standard American English? Basically, is the \"safest\" way to ensure a witness is taken seriously by a jury to essentially avoid any dialectal markers that might trigger those subconscious biases you mentioned?",
