      "content": "Yes, the safest strategy to ensure a witness is taken seriously is to strictly adhere to Standard American English and completely avoid any dialectal markers or slang.\nJuries are notoriously biased against non-standard speech, often assuming that witnesses who speak with an accent or use colloquialisms are less intelligent, less honest, or even criminal.\nBy eliminating these linguistic features, you can effectively neutralize the subconscious prejudice that would otherwise cause a jury to dismiss the witness's testimony as unreliable.",
